what REDS %767 named its own gap in its second field: 'Not a guard -- nothing in this tree asks whether every field a contract publishes carries a ceiling that contract declares.' Four fields of the accepted receipt contract refused at mantra/src/tally_receipt_offer_bounds.rye's max_identifier_bytes=96, a number the contract declared for each identifier and for none of them; a water-row reading caught it, and no instrument could. Build the reading that holds the contract's ceiling table and the code's per-field application to one answer: parse the | field | ceiling | unit | rows of active-designing/20260912-201126_the-receipt-you-can-read-contract.md, parse the max_* constants of the bounds module, extract from fact_refusal in mantra/src/receipt_offer.rye every field name and the constant it is refused at, and gate unnamed_ceiling and value_disagrees at zero. Report the structural cause %767's repair left standing: the contract declares a population row for each identifier and never enumerates its members, which is the hole product_digest fell through. Report a declared ceiling no code site enforces -- receipt_card_width and receipt_card_height stand at 72 and 18 and are read by nothing. No behavior change, no number moved; the four derivations stay Keaton's word under the contract's own closing clause.
